== mojolearn.tests.test_svr_surface ==
   surface mojolearn.SVR (svm/, epsilon-SVR)

  PROVENANCE
    pass the loaded binary exports svr_fit
    pass the loaded binary exports svr_predict
    pass the binary reports a tier it knows

  REFUSALS
    pass kernel='poly' is refused by name
    pass kernel='sigmoid' is refused by name
    pass kernel='precomputed' is refused by name
    pass an unknown kernel name is refused
    pass gamma='scale' is refused and names the deviation
    pass an unknown gamma name is refused
    pass a negative gamma is refused
    pass degree is refused, naming the kernel that would read it
    pass coef0 is refused, naming the kernels that would read it
    pass a non-positive C is refused
    pass a non-finite C is refused
    pass a non-positive tol is refused
    pass a non-positive cache_size is refused
    pass max_iter=0 is refused
    pass a negative nochange_steps is refused
    pass verbose is refused, naming what it would have selected
    pass output_type is refused
    pass shrinking is not a parameter of this class and says so
    pass sample_weight is refused in fit()
    pass a 2-D y is refused
    pass a y of the wrong length is refused
    pass a 1-D X is refused
    pass predict before fit is refused
    pass a predict X with the wrong width is refused
    pass a negative epsilon is refused BY THE SOLVER'S scope check
    pass a non-finite epsilon is refused BY THE SOLVER'S scope check
    pass a NaN target is refused BY NAME with its index (DEVIATION 636)
    pass a non-finite X cell is refused BY NAME (DEVIATION 636)

  PLANTED
    pass the fit found at least one support vector
    pass n_features_in_ is the width of X
    pass n_iter_ came back positive
    pass coef_ recovers the planted weights
    pass intercept_ recovers the planted offset
    pass predict reproduces the training targets to the noise floor
    pass score() is a high R^2 on a noiseless fit
    pass kernel='rbf' fits the same problem (its own two kernels run)

  TUBE
    pass n_support_ does not grow from epsilon=0.0000 to 0.0200
    pass n_support_ does not grow from epsilon=0.0200 to 0.0600
    pass n_support_ does not grow from epsilon=0.0600 to 0.1500
    pass n_support_ does not grow from epsilon=0.1500 to 0.5000
    pass the widest tube is STRICTLY smaller than the narrowest
    pass every NON-support row lies inside the tube
    pass a narrow tube still fits
    pass the widest tube does not fit BETTER than the narrow one

  SHAPES
    pass n_support_ is at most n_rows, never 2 * n_rows
    pass dual_coef_ is (1, n_support_)
    pass support_ is (n_support_,)
    pass support_vectors_ is (n_support_, n_features)
    pass intercept_ is (1,)
    pass the model arrays are float32
    pass support_ is int32
    pass every support index is a row of X
    pass the support indices are distinct and ascending
    pass support_vectors_ ARE the rows support_ names
    pass every folded dual coefficient is bounded by C
    pass coef_ raises AttributeError for a non-linear kernel

  INVARIANCE
    pass [REPORT, not asserted] row 7 alone == row 7 inside the full call: MOVED -- 1 of 1 cells differ; first at flat index 0, 0x3f30e8d0 vs 0x3f30e8d8
    pass [REPORT, not asserted] rows 40:73 as a block == the same rows inside the full call: same
    pass [REPORT, not asserted] the whole matrix through a 0.001038 MiB predict buffer == one batch: same
    pass [REPORT, not asserted] kernel='linear': row 99 alone == row 99 in the batch: MOVED -- 1 of 1 cells differ; first at flat index 0, 0xbd5fdda0 vs 0xbd5fed40

  GAMMA
    pass 'auto' resolves to 1 / n_features
    pass [REPORT, not asserted] gamma='auto' == the same number written out: same
    pass gamma='auto' agrees with the same number to float32 tolerance in EVERY tier
    pass a DIFFERENT gamma gives a different answer, so the row above is not vacuous

